y></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MAKINO TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MASAI KENTARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUNO SUNIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAJI KAZUFUMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWASAKI, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MAKINO, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MASAI, KENTARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUNO, SUNIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAJI, KAZUFUMI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A car body, in which a hollow shape stock composed of two face plates and ribs joining the face plates together is used to form a side body, and stresses are reduced while minimizing an increase in mass. A car body, comprising a hollow shape stock composed of two face plates (31, 31) and ribs (32) joining the face plates together and used to form a side body (11), wherein face plate portions (31c, 31d) in regions (B, D) above and below connection points (c) between circular arcs, which constitute corner portions of a window (15), and vertical sides of the window (15) are greater in thickness than in the remaining regions (A, C, E). Stresses are most heavily concentrated in the regions (B, D). Therefore, it is possible to achieve reduction in mass and enhancement in strength together. Further, buckling preventive tools can be arranged in spaces in the regions (B, D) of the hollow shape stock. Further, with the hollow shape stock (18) in a pier panel, face plates on an internal side are greater in thickness than those on an external side.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Carrosserie automobile mettant en application une forme creuse composée de deux plaques avant et de nervures accouplant lesdites plaques, afin de constituer une partie latérale, ce qui permet de réduire les contraintes, tout en limitant au maximum l'augmentation de masse. Cette carrosserie présente une forme creuse composée de deux plaques avant (31, 31) et de nervures (32) accouplant ces plaques avant afin de constituer une partie latérale (11), des parties (31c, 31d) des plaques avant dans des zones (B, D) situées au-dessus et au-dessous de points d'accouplement (c) entre des arcs de cercle constituant les coins d'une fenêtre (15) et les côtés verticaux de la fenêtre (15), présentant une épaisseur supérieure à celle des autres zones (A, C, E). Les contraintes se concentrent plus particulièrement dans les zones (B, D). Cette conception permet de diminuer la masse et d'augmenter la résistance de la carrosserie. De plus, des éléments empêchant le plissement peuvent être placés dans des espaces des zones (B, D) de la forme creuse. Cette dernière, dans le panneau de support vertical entre fenêtres, permet également à l'épaisseur des plaques avant côté intérieur d'être supérieure à celle des plaques avant côté extérieur.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>